    "narrative": "For this June 24th slate, our strongest plays are anchored by **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Lawrence Butler** (68.54). **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Miles Mikolas, where a +16% SP skill adjustment and a +13% platoon boost push him into the elite tier. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** is a high-value play; despite the park penalty, the combination of a favorable SP matchup and wind blowing out at the venue provides the leverage needed to exploit his power profile. **Daulton Varsho** also rounds out our high-output options (65.71) as his power-speed blend matches up well against the pitching profile of Mike Burrows.\n\nRegarding bench decisions, **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.32) was the final man left out, narrowly missing the cut behind **Masyn Winn**. While **Jung Hoo Lee** benefits from a slight wind-out boost, his platoon disadvantage against the lefty Gage Jump ultimately suppressed his score below our threshold for starting consideration. We are playing it cautious with **Tyler Freeman** (57.69) today; while his park factor is excellent (+14%), he faces a challenging outing against Ranger Suarez, and his score reflects the volatility of that matchup. Please note that we remain at the mercy of pending lineups for several players, most notably **Yainer Diaz**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Jonathan Aranda**; any shifts in their batting order will require a recalibration of their efficiency scores. Finally, the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a significant blow to our daily ceiling, forcing us to rely on high-volume consistency from the rest of the lineup to compensate for his missing production.",
